## POD URI HANDLING — attached media / artifacts as edge targets

A sentence may contain a token of the shape `datapod:<kind>:<id>`
(e.g., `datapod:image:abc12345...`, `datapod:video:def67890...`,
`datapod:email:ghi...`). These are ALREADY-EXISTING node ids — the
attached image / video / email / etc. has been minted as a "Pod" node
in the KG via a separate ingest path. You are NOT a separate `entity`
node for the pod; you are referencing an existing node by id.

**Treat the URI as a target_id (or source_id) verbatim:**
- Do NOT mint a new node for the pod. Do NOT use it as a "label".
- Do NOT split or paraphrase the URI. Pass it through exactly as it appears.
- The URI substitutes for a temp_id when constructing edges.

**Edge-type vocabulary for pod targets, by kind:**

| Pod kind | Default-safe edge | Intent-flavored upgrades |
|---|---|---|
| image | `depicted_in` | `has_profile_image` (when user calls it their/Katy's/etc. profile or canonical photo), `has_screenshot`, `has_receipt` (transaction docs) |
| video | `depicted_in` | `has_video`, `has_recording` |
| audio | `mentioned_in` | `has_recording`, `has_voicemail` |
| email | `mentioned_in` | `invoiced_via`, `replied_to` |
| chat_cluster | `discussed_in` | (rare; mostly historical reference) |

**Direction: KG-node → Pod**, always. Edge runs FROM the entity / event / state node TO the pod URI. Reads as "Jukka is depicted in this pod" / "Peter's Birth has this video."

**Default-safe rule:** when the user's framing is ambiguous, emit the kind's default edge. When the framing is clearly possessive/canonical ("here is my profile picture", "use this as my photo"), ALSO emit the intent-flavored edge alongside the default. One canonical (`has_profile_image`) edge per entity is the convention; many `depicted_in` edges from anywhere is fine.

### Pod URI examples

**"Here is a picture of me datapod:image:abc12345xyz9000123def"**
- Speaker is the user; "of me" → speaker is depicted; "here is a picture of me" framing is ambiguous between casual and canonical.
- Nodes:
    * temp_id: "entity_1", label: "{{ resource_user_data.preferred_name }}", node_type: "Entity", sentence: "Here is a picture of {{ resource_user_data.preferred_name }} datapod:image:abc12345xyz9000123def"
- Edges:
    * source: "entity_1", target: "datapod:image:abc12345xyz9000123def", label: "depicted_in", sentence: "{{ resource_user_data.preferred_name }} is depicted in this image."

**"Here is my profile picture datapod:image:def67890..."**
- "my profile picture" is the canonical framing — emit BOTH default and intent-flavored.
- Edges:
    * source: "entity_1", target: "datapod:image:def67890...", label: "depicted_in", sentence: "{{ resource_user_data.preferred_name }} is depicted in this image."
    * source: "entity_1", target: "datapod:image:def67890...", label: "has_profile_image", sentence: "{{ resource_user_data.preferred_name }}'s profile image is this image."

**"Video of Peter's birthday party datapod:video:abc..."**
- An event-anchored video; the event itself is the natural source of the `has_video` edge.
- Nodes:
    * temp_id: "entity_1", label: "Peter", node_type: "Entity"
    * temp_id: "event_1", label: "Birthday Party", node_type: "Event", sentence: "Peter's birthday party."
- Edges:
    * source: "entity_1", target: "event_1", label: "honoree", sentence: "Peter is the honoree of the birthday party."
    * source: "event_1", target: "datapod:video:abc...", label: "has_video", sentence: "The birthday party has a video."
    * source: "entity_1", target: "datapod:video:abc...", label: "depicted_in", sentence: "Peter is depicted in this video."

**"Receipt from Chipotle datapod:image:ghi..."**
- Receipt → `has_receipt` is the intent-flavored upgrade; the underlying transaction is the anchor.
- Nodes:
    * temp_id: "entity_1", label: "Chipotle", node_type: "Entity"
